WEBVTT

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:32.970
Moose!

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:37.850
That's impossible, sir.

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:40.470
They're about 4-500 meters away.

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:44.020
And they're also downwind. They're sure to get our scent.

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:48.360
If you're just trying to spook them, you should stop right now.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.360
Ahh, we blew it.

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:55.150
They noticed us.

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:10.000
Sounds like a hunter.

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:11.340
And he's close.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:11.750
Mm-hmm.

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:16.590
And I thought we didn't have any poachers in this area.

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:17.760
Anyways, let's check it out.

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:27.900
You... You got two!

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:32.730
And you only shot your gun once.

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:38.870
Oh shoot!

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:47.290
Bob!

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:55.920
Bob Miller, park ranger for this game area. May we see your hunting permit?

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:02.760
Duke Togo...

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:05.730
Looks like you're not from around here.

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:06.770
Where did you come from?

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:11.560
They were supposed to tell you this when you got your hunting permit:

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:17.280
Only one moose is allowed per hunter in this area.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:18.610
Kuki!

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:22.660
How come you didn't tell him, if you're a competent guide?

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:25.410
H-Hold on, officer!

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:28.410
He only shot his gun once!

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.790
I swear, it was a complete accident!

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:32.840
What did you say?

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:42.680
Bob, this is unreal. It's just like Kuki said.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:45.260
That's right, we only heard one gunshot.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:51.850
Well, in any case, you still broke the law.

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:55.940
You will have your license suspended and be forced to pay a fine.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:03:00.200
You'll need to come with us to the rangers' station.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:07.410
Don't move!

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:10.330
So you're resisting?

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:13.330
Kuki! Take the man's rifle!

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:27.310
Who is this guy?

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:36.980
You only had to pay a few hundred dollars in fines.
Now you got yourself into a fine bit of trouble.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:46.910
I walk unsteadily on paths to nowhere

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:47.370
Doutei Subs Presents:

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:51.040
wondering what I should do right now.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:57.500
I play the song you like on the car stereo

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:02.050
with the volume up and my feelings crystallized

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:07.680
driving on streets with no crossroads or signals

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:13.100
with a speed that will catch up with you.

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:17.570
So faraway - let's run!

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:23.860
And let's not bother with the breaks - full throttle.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:28.160
Oh someday - one of these days

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:33.250
You'll be at my place where nobody can find you.

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:39.340
Whenever you suffer a breakdown one can't see

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:44.930
depend on me for your repairs.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:49.310
So faraway - let's run!

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:55.520
We'll reset and start again - even at our limit.

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:59.820
Oh someday - one of these days

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:05.820
If I'm with you we'll find our dream.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:16.040
On Large Mouth Lake

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:22.710
There were about six or seven of them!

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:26.510
And those gigantic moose were like specks on the horizon!

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:28.680
And he still brought them down?

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:30.470
While they were running?

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:33.770
Yeah, and with only one shot!

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:41.480
What's really amazing is that the bullet went through one's throat then buried itself in the chest of another one!

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:46.990
However, we got unlucky and caught the attention of the park rangers.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:51.410
They probably aren't going to let him go home tonight.

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:02.130
Get ready to leave.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.920
You found him?

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:08.800
Haven't seen him for myself, but it has to be him.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:10.300
Let's go!

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:11.010
Mm-hmm.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:20.100
So...

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:25.740
Where the hell is he at?

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:27.450
The park ranger's office.

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:29.450
So that means he'll be unarmed.

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:30.700
Mm-hmm.

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:32.490
Still...

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:32.950
Hmm?

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:36.450
I never thought we'd find him this soon.

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:40.710
He calls the attention of people wherever he goes.

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:46.460
That's because he's Golgo 13... an Übermensch of a pro.

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:51.720
If we let this chance slip away, we'll be the ones who will go down.

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:55.470
If we all want to come back alive, we must have his head on a mount.

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:13.910
Hey!

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:19.000
When are you going to say something?

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:27.840
Yes... his name is Duke Togo.

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:33.340
He appears to be of Japanese descent, but he has yet to say anything during the interrogation.

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:34.800
No.

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:39.640
All he has is a map Large Mouth Lake plus his other effects, nothing that's illegal in Canada.

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:42.350
Yes, understood.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:46.770
It's no gun I've ever seen.

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:50.280
Yeah, it's too heavy to be a hunting rifle.

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:53.160
It looks custom-made along with the bullets.

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:55.320
Hmm...

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:56.870
I get it.

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:02.370
It looks like you're not just some average hunter.

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:03.710
Hey! I'm asking you one more time...

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:05.960
Where did you come from?

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:08.710
Why did you come to this area?

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:12.720
Dammit!

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:14.220
You better shape up!

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:16.850
Hey Burke, will you give that a rest?

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:19.720
But Bob, we aren't getting anywhere!

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:28.400
That's him! That's Golgo 13!

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:32.490
Plus they got both his hands in cuffs!

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:33.530
Good.

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:38.830
Be sure you have the car at the entrance ten seconds after we storm the station.

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:39.700
Got it?

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:40.910
Loud and clear.

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:55.840
We can forget about your motive.

00:08:56.470 --> 00:09:01.600
We'll just make requests for your personal data to our Ottawa offices and the Japanese embassy in the morning.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:04.230
Hmm?

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:05.520
Who's there?

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:13.440
Burke!

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:21.240
What is this?!

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:46.390
Burke! Hang on!

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:48.190
I'll get you first aid!

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:54.400
Luckily, it looks like the bullet went right through.

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:56.150
Hmm?

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:10.670
Wait, Togo!

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:18.880
Drive!

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:27.180
Do it now!

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:31.560
Wait!

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:39.240
That man really wasn't any ordinary Joe.

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:42.240
So what motive did he have coming here?

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:12.860
Did you get anything on those guys?

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:15.320
Burke! You should still be in bed.

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:21.530
The medication wore off, and it got too painful to sleep.

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:23.450
So what are we looking at?

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:25.870
Well...

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:28.540
I ran the usual check on those guys.

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:32.540
But I haven't found anything that can ID them.

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:36.420
So now we got a mystery on our hands.

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:42.010
Togo who just escaped, coupled with these guys... we're not just dealing with any regular criminals.

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:50.060
What are they... trying to do around here?

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:19.880
I've brought some hot water.

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:20.920
Thank you.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:25.010
How is your wife doing?

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:28.140
Oh, she's sound asleep.

00:12:32.690 --> 00:12:36.110
Okay, if you need anything, give me a call.

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:08.390
<i>Is this... to keep me from escaping?</i>

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:20.190
Th... That lousy...

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:23.690
Huh?

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:15.870
<i>Idiot.</i>

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:20.210
<i>Did you think that I would actually inhale that knock-out drug now that I'm awake?</i>

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:06.840
You called me, sir?

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:10.760
Can you clean up in the kitchen while I'm out?

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:15.220
That's quite all right!

00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:19.640
I've already received these fine clothes from you.

00:15:20.690 --> 00:15:22.150
I'll leave it to you then.

00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:24.440
I'll see you later!

00:16:01.940 --> 00:16:02.440
Hmm?

00:16:11.150 --> 00:16:12.910
Yes, that's right.

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:15.280
Forgive me for my delayed contact.

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:16.910
I see.

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:19.040
So you're the only one left?

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:22.160
Anyway, you must quickly get to Point L.

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:24.120
We'll call Troika about the current situation.

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:28.420
We will protect Troika's life from "G" no matter what!

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:30.300
Yes, understood.

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:32.590
I'll figure out something.

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:14.470
Considering the circumstances, we need to hit this target over a very long distance with just one shot.

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:19.760
We will fully comply with your terms for taking on this assignment.

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:26.020
His name is Joseph D. McCord.

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:29.400
He used to be a cryptanalyst for our CIA branch office.

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:34.650
However, we recently discovered that he was actually a double agent.

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:40.330
McCord disappeared from Yellowknife once we blew his cover.

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:43.750
We're still unable to accurately pinpoint his current location.

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:48.580
He's trying to defect to the embassy in Ottawa.

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:52.750
He is currently waiting for his comrades to retrieve him via a helicopter.

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:59.510
His retrieval will occur on the surface of a small lake called Large Mouth.

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:05.770
In other words, you will only have a moment's contact with your target on Large Mouth Lake.

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:10.440
We don't have the time to get you any other point of contact.

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:12.610
We would like to hear your response.

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:28.790
Hmm?

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:45.180
<i>I have to get to Large Mouth.</i>

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:49.480
<i>I have a hunch that I'll find all my answers there.</i>

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:05.830
Hmm?

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:07.540
Who's there?!

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:15.130
I'm here to take Troika to Point L!

00:19:17.960 --> 00:19:19.380
Glad you made it.

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:23.180
The battery died on my communicator box so I couldn't use it.

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:26.220
Plus my feet got frostbite, I thought I was done for.

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:31.730
Your retrieval is still going according to plan.

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:34.980
Your helicopter is about to arrive, McCord.

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:38.190
We must leave here immediately.

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:41.860
The CIA has hired a sniper to take you out.

00:19:58.210 --> 00:19:58.920
Hmm?

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:03.840
It's here!

00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:06.140
Your express trip to Ottawa!

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:09.350
Thank God.

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:14.060
It came earlier than expected, but it looks like they've spotted us anyway.

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:16.110
Yeah, you got that right.

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:20.150
Anyone can make you with that bright red down jacket you got on.

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:22.110
Even if they are a bit of ways away.

00:20:28.910 --> 00:20:31.040
Anyone can make me?

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:35.540
<i>Come to think of it...</i>

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:40.800
<i>...slipping away from Golgo 13 was almost too easy.</i>

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:45.390
<i>Almost too easy...</i>

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:48.760
<i>Why?</i>

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:57.520
<i>A trap!</i>

00:20:58.060 --> 00:20:59.400
<i>It might be a trap!</i>

00:21:02.360 --> 00:21:04.610
Wait! Don't go onto Large Mouth Lake!

00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:05.320
Hmm?

00:21:44.440 --> 00:21:45.400
It's him.

00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:51.830
It was by no coincidence or luck that the took down those two moose with one shot.

00:21:57.540 --> 00:21:58.920
It was all for this.

00:22:43.840 --> 00:22:47.130
I  was worried with no one to talk to.

00:22:47.130 --> 00:22:50.180
I was brooding and standing still

00:22:50.180 --> 00:22:52.350
without moving a muscle.

00:22:53.010 --> 00:22:55.520
I wonder when that was?

00:22:56.020 --> 00:22:57.230
I'm sure

00:22:57.230 --> 00:23:00.400
you agonized over how

00:23:00.400 --> 00:23:05.650
people will hurt themselves and other people

00:23:06.280 --> 00:23:08.900
and fail to realize it.

00:23:09.280 --> 00:23:10.030
When

00:23:10.030 --> 00:23:13.450
the same days keep repeating themselves

00:23:13.450 --> 00:23:15.700
you never change.

00:23:16.410 --> 00:23:17.950
Since you're here for me

00:23:17.950 --> 00:23:22.250
I will accept the way that I am.

00:23:22.960 --> 00:23:26.500
I will never leave you alone

00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:29.840
I will softly touch your trembling heart.

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:36.720
I realized that I'm not the only one who's alone.

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:39.890
We're enveloped in the gentle sun beams.

00:23:39.890 --> 00:23:43.230
The long winter is finally over.

00:23:43.230 --> 00:23:49.860
The parts of us that were lonely will surely get stronger.

00:24:02.040 --> 00:24:04.920
Golgo lost his memories.

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:10.760
Together with the woman who rescued him, he begins to search for clues and fragments

00:24:10.760 --> 00:24:13.800
to who he really is.

00:24:14.430 --> 00:24:20.430
Will his sniper instincts help him recall the assignment concealed within him?

00:24:20.310 --> 00:24:25.810
The Lost Assignment

00:24:20.430 --> 00:24:24.020
Next time on Golgo 13: The Lost Assignment.

00:24:24.020 --> 00:24:28.400
Don't stand behind him, if you value your life.
